From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Feb 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: fold the players of Card, Group and Effect functions
 for n > 2

Lua gives these functions a folded player: 0 is the duelist who runs the script, 1 is an opponent.
Before this change they used that value as a real seat.

Card functions: the viewer argument of card info (GetCode, GetType, IsType, IsRace and others) is unfolded.
IsControler, IsPreviousControler and IsSummonPlayer match through fold::matches.
GetOwner, GetPreviousControler, GetReasonPlayer and GetSummonPlayer push a folded player.
The zone functions, the overlay and counter functions, IsHasEffect, RemoveCounter and the Is-able-to functions unfold the player.
A value that is not a living duelist gives the stock invalid result.
SetReasonPlayer accepts a duelist, none or all.

Group functions: Select, FilterSelect, SelectUnselect, SelectWithSumEqual and SelectWithSumGreater unfold the chooser.
RandomSelect does the same.
No prompt goes to an eliminated or non-duelist seat.

Effect functions: SetOwnerPlayer unfolds. GetOwnerPlayer and GetHandlerPlayer push a folded player.
SetAbsoluteRange: in FFA it compares the named player with the effect owner.
In Tag the stock rule stands, because the Lua value is the team id and team 0 is the s side.
IsActivatable and the count limit functions unfold the player.

The n == 2 path is the stock code, so the bytes do not change.
Left as is: functions with no Lua player and functions that only pass a value through.
Card.GetControl is a Duel row and stays for the Duel rows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UrYy4jjEcbJHKdcVYasfdb
